WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.339
So this is a super interesting story that
is getting a lot of attention in the last

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:06.339
24 hours.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.700
I was even on rising this morning talking
about this with crystal ball and cigar and

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:17.780
jetty and the story is that how speaker Nancy
Pelosi, of course, a Democrat said yesterday

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.930
that she would be comfortable with Bernie
Sanders as the democratic presidential nominee

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:29.450
if indeed he ends up being the selection of
the democratic primary voters in what's left

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.420
of this 2020 democratic primary.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.540
And she was asked this just as she was walking
out of a meeting of the house of representatives

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.480
and she simply said yes, answering the question.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.570
Yes she would be comfortable.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.200
And this is interesting for a few different
reasons and before we go on with the discussion,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.570
also note that Senate minority leader, Chuck
Schumer was asked a similar question and he

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.630
sort of seemed to be saying the same thing.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.030
He said, quote, look, the bottom line is very
simple.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.360
We have a lot of strong nominees and I'm not
supporting one over the other, but I think

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.159
every one of them will be a will beat president
Trump or would be better than president Trump.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:11.020
So not a ringing endorsement, but certainly
both Schumer and Pelosi, the democratic leaders

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.109
in the respective house, Senate and house
are saying they would at least be okay with

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:16.439
a Bernie Sanders nomination.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.009
So there's a few different angles here to
talk about.

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:20.009
First of all is okay.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:25.869
I mean they, they recognize that Bernie of
all the candidates has the clearest path to

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:26.969
the nomination.

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:31.220
It's certainly clearer than any other individual
candidate right now.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.689
And so they're just getting in line.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:37.759
This is a relatively cynical interpretation,
but I think one that is not a irrationally

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:40.499
cynical, they want to be on the inside, not
the outside.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:42.929
If Bernie Sanders ends up as the nominee.

00:01:42.929 --> 00:01:45.439
And in particular, if Bernie Sanders ends
up being president.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:50.799
So in one sense you could say, we don't really
have to pay much attention to Pelosi and Schumer

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:57.669
saying this because it is a cynical, strategic
decision of the centrist establishment Democrats,

00:01:57.669 --> 00:02:02.479
uh, to make sure that they don't end up getting
the door shut on them.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:04.990
If Bernie Sanders becomes nominee or president.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.319
And that's obviously part of it.

00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:11.439
There is no question that they don't want
to be on the outside if Bernie's the nominee.

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:14.640
But there's a very important secondary implication
here.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:22.170
Uh, if you look at the five 38 odds right
now, there are roughly equal odds of Bernie

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:30.349
securing the nomination before the DNC with
1,991 delegates or more and roughly equal

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:34.440
odds of there being nobody who gets to 50%
plus one.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:40.989
If there is nobody who gets to 50% plus one
delegates before the DNC, the democratic establishment

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:46.220
is going to need to decide whether they want
to contest the convention and try to deny

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:52.440
Bernie Sanders the nomination either through
the Alliance of the delegates of various centers,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.659
candidates or with the addition of the superdelegates
on the second round of voting who could just

00:02:56.659 --> 00:02:59.099
hand the nomination to somebody else.

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:05.219
So the importance of Nancy Pelosi and Schumer
signaling, or at least though Kay, with a

00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:11.940
Bernie nomination, maybe a sign that the democratic
establishment is not going to try to contest

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:17.120
or broker the convention in order to deny
Bernie the nomination, even if he has a plurality

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.510
of the delegates.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:23.120
That in and of itself is a crucial decision
because that could have a huge effect on the

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.299
general election.

00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:30.620
It is conceivable that if the democratic party
is seen as heavy handed and going out of their

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:36.519
way to deny the nomination to the person with
the most delegates, if that person is indeed

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:40.720
Bernie Sanders, there is a risk that that
is going to reduce turnout in November and

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.989
help Donald Trump win.

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:48.079
It is a risk that it will turn some democratic
voters who support Bernie Sanders in the primary

00:03:48.079 --> 00:03:53.510
away from voting at all in November or even
towards writing somebody in third party, uh,

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.959
to voting for Donald Trump even.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:59.490
And when you start to see party leaders saying
things like Nancy Pelosi saying, I'd be comfortable

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.439
with Bernie as the nominee.

00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:06.230
This could be a very important sign that they
recognize that it could be a self-destructive

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:11.549
action to take the nomination from Bernie
Sanders or to be seen as doing that even if

00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:13.150
it's not in practice.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.420
What you believe is going on now at the same
time, uh, could it, this could be something

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:24.100
that is being said by Pelosi and Schumer to
make us think they won't contest the convention

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.800
when in fact they plan to.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.050
But that's sort of like two layers of cynicism.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.870
Maybe it's too much cynicism.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.690
There's also a potential lesson here from
Republicans in 2016 because when you think

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:40.970
back to the Republican primary in 2016 remember
that for a whole bunch of that primary, the

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:46.800
full Republican establishment, including Fox
news and a lot of right wing media, they were

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.940
United against Donald Trump instead of with
Donald Trump.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:56.360
Now they ultimately came around to him because
anything was better than Hillary in their

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.360
eyes.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.580
And Donald Trump ended out just barely squeaking
out an electoral college victory because of

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.200
about 77,000 votes in three key States.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.990
It's not crazy to think that if the DNC were
to simply rally behind whoever is the nominee,

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:17.480
uh, and even behind whoever is looking like
they have the best shot at being the nominee,

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.940
which right now is Bernie.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:23.990
They might be saying, even if we don't like
Bernie, even if we're not actually comfortable

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:29.250
with Bernie as the nominee, if Republicans
were able to get Trump elected even after

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:34.030
being against them almost all the primary
and coming to him at the end, maybe our best

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:39.580
shot at removing Trump is just getting behind
whoever is the nominee, regardless of whether

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.120
they are from what they perceive to be a different
wing of the left or the democratic party.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:49.730
In the end, it's important that Nancy Pelosi
is even willing to say this at this point

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:53.880
in time, even if it's completely cynical,
even if it's completely self-serving and out

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.850
of her motivation, not to end up on the outside
of the democratic party.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:03.260
If indeed Bernie Sanders becomes the nominee
or president, it is still important that she's

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.800
saying this at this point in time.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:10.320
If you have a different interpretation of
what Pelosi and Schumer signaling, at least

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.560
acquiescing to the idea of a Bernie Sanders
candidacy, let me know.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:14.573
I do want to hear from you.

